WEBVTT

00:00:15.020 --> 00:00:15.800
How are you?

00:00:17.240 --> 00:00:18.080
Fine, thank you.

00:00:18.220 --> 00:00:19.980
This is my friend Harry Bennett.

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:22.560
Very nice to meet you.

00:00:25.640 --> 00:00:26.440
Follow me, please.

00:00:28.620 --> 00:00:30.780
I do, too. I come here often.

00:00:43.310 --> 00:00:46.950
Would you like something to drink?

00:00:47.280 --> 00:00:49.800
Yes, I'd like a glass of ginger ale with ice.

00:00:50.020 --> 00:00:51.080
Harry, what would you like?

00:00:52.040 --> 00:00:53.800
Do you have a dry white wine?

00:00:54.040 --> 00:00:55.540
How about a California chablis?

00:00:55.600 --> 00:00:56.580
Chablis is fine.

00:00:57.370 --> 00:00:58.780
What would you like to eat?

00:01:01.700 --> 00:01:03.240
Harry, would you like to see a menu?

00:01:09.640 --> 00:01:10.680
What is it?

00:01:12.460 --> 00:01:14.940
Crispy fried noodles. I love them.

00:01:15.400 --> 00:01:16.880
May I bring you a salad?

00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:17.840
Oh yes.

00:01:18.340 --> 00:01:19.500
What do you recommend today?

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:21.600
I recommend rose-petal salad.

00:01:21.860 --> 00:01:23.100
Special for new friends.

00:01:24.060 --> 00:01:25.400
Rose-petal salad?

00:01:26.500 --> 00:01:27.140
Why not?

00:01:27.700 --> 00:01:29.280
I'll take care of everything.

00:01:32.500 --> 00:01:35.160
I hope you're hungry.

00:01:46.900 --> 00:01:49.560
What do you do at Universe Toy Company?

00:01:49.900 --> 00:01:52.500
I'm the vice-president of new toy development.

00:01:52.880 --> 00:01:53.940
Terrific!

00:01:54.860 --> 00:01:56.700
I know you 're a CPA.

00:01:57.260 --> 00:01:59.300
That's true. Harry Bennett,

00:01:59.420 --> 00:02:00.540
certified public accountant.

00:02:01.040 --> 00:02:02.180
I love numbers.

00:02:02.400 --> 00:02:04.180
I do some work for Smith and Dale,

00:02:06.720 --> 00:02:07.900
And so...

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:10.100
Here we are.

00:02:10.840 --> 00:02:11.540
Yes.

00:02:12.340 --> 00:02:13.420
I have a daughter.

00:02:13.820 --> 00:02:15.660
I know. How old is she?

00:02:15.920 --> 00:02:17.180
She's nine years old.

00:02:17.380 --> 00:02:19.560
That's a nice age. What's her name?

00:02:19.730 --> 00:02:20.190
Michelle.

00:02:20.760 --> 00:02:22.720
Do you have a picture of her?

00:02:33.400 --> 00:02:34.920
She's very pretty.

00:02:35.560 --> 00:02:37.080
Thank you.

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.420
And there's a phone call for you, Mr. Bennett.

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:53.840
I hope nothing is wrong.

00:02:54.580 --> 00:02:56.100
I'll get the rest of the dinner.

00:02:56.260 --> 00:02:56.860
Excuse me.

00:03:09.920 --> 00:03:12.040
Please forgive me, Susan, but...

00:03:16.500 --> 00:03:17.580
What's the matter?

00:03:18.200 --> 00:03:19.900
My daughter isn't feeling well.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:21.860
Oh no! Is it serious?

00:03:22.960 --> 00:03:26.480
I don't know. The baby-sitter says she has a stomachache,

00:03:26.480 --> 00:03:27.180
and she's crying.

00:03:27.540 --> 00:03:28.400
I'll have to go home.

00:03:29.640 --> 00:03:32.540
Of course. I'm so sorry for Michelle.

00:03:33.300 --> 00:03:35.020
And you didn't have a chance to eat.

00:03:36.000 --> 00:03:37.320
Let me take you home first.

00:03:37.420 --> 00:03:39.180
No, no. Please, go ahead.

00:03:39.780 --> 00:03:41.060
It's our first date.

00:03:42.160 --> 00:03:43.360
We'll make another.

00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:44.600
Please don't worry.

00:03:45.770 --> 00:03:47.640
I'll phone you.
